by nicolas-grekas at 2026-08-05T11:38:16Z

Rebuilt on your plan @Amoifr and pushed, rebased on 8.2. Thanks for stopping to agree the direction first, it was the right call.

What landed follows your write-up: `ChoiceView::$help` filled by `DefaultChoiceListFactory` with the same per-choice resolution as `$label`, `ChoiceList::help()` plus a `Cache\ChoiceHelp` wrapper so the view stays cached, `$help` added to `ChoiceListFactoryInterface::createView()` as a commented parameter read through `func_get_args()`, `choice_attr` untouched, translation through `choice_translation_domain`, and no `choice_help_html`.

Three things on top:

The parameter goes last in the `ChoiceView` constructor, after `$labelTranslationParameters`, so positional construction keeps working. Symfony's own implementations repeat `@param array|callable|null $help` in their docblocks: `DebugClassLoader` reads the `@param` on the interface and deprecates every implementation that declares neither, which would otherwise have added three self-deprecations to a suite that runs with `max[total]=0`.

Rendering covers all seven themes that define `choice_widget_expanded`, not four. `bootstrap_base`, `bootstrap_4` and `daisyui_5` override the block too, so leaving them out would have made the option silently do nothing there.

Each child gets `aria-describedby` pointing at its help element. That is the part `choice_attr` cannot do today, and it is the argument for the option existing, so it is worth keeping in whatever the docs end up saying.

Tests assert on rendered output this time: three in `FormExtensionDivLayoutTest`, four in `ChoiceTypeTest`, three in `CachingFactoryDecoratorTest`. Verified by mutation, each fails alone when its piece is reverted, including the caching one and the `aria-describedby` wiring. Form 4945 green, Twig bridge 1992 green, no new deprecations.

Collapsed selects render nothing, by construction rather than as a shortcut, and the description says so. Still needs a docs PR.
